1
00:00:00,021 --> 00:00:06,032
Sleep or Serum: before you buy that eye cream, check last night.

2
00:00:06,032 --> 00:00:12,243
Judges can try Sample mode for free: it replays a real, recorded YouCam API result.

3
00:00:12,243 --> 00:00:19,227
Step 2: how long did you sleep? The sky gets darker as the night gets shorter.

4
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:23,240
Step 3: what were you about to buy? Here: an eye cream for dark circles.

5
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:30,780
Look in the mirror. In live mode this uploads the photo and polls the YouCam skin-analysis task.

6
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:35,291
Five SD concerns from YouCam: dark circles, eye bags, droopy upper eyelid, radiance and age spots.

7
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:41,297
Verdict: dark circles are sleep-sensitive and the night was short, so sleep 3 good nights first.

8
00:00:41,297 --> 00:00:47,305
No black box: every rule the app checked is listed, with the cut-offs it used.

9
00:00:47,305 --> 00:00:56,387
Slept 8 hours instead? Sleep is not the likely fix, so the app suggests a product category.

10
00:00:56,387 --> 00:01:02,409
Age spots are not sleep-sensitive, so the verdict says: choose a product for it. Categories only, no brands.

11
00:01:02,409 --> 00:01:11,422
Every sleep claim cites peer-reviewed research, and the app says clearly: not medical advice.

12
00:01:11,422 --> 00:01:20,452
Under the hood: YouCam File API upload, skin-analysis task, then polling. The API key stays on the server.

13
00:01:20,452 --> 00:01:25,462
Sleep or Serum: sleep first, or buy with confidence.
